export anchor VinylSleeveStyle:
    number: 92
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Vinyl sleeve
    idea: The home screen is a 70s record sleeve with the greeting as the album title, the fortnight pressed into a pale vinyl disc as groove wedges, and the projects listed as tracks on side A and side B.
    base: light
    palette:
        shop: #efebe3, the page
        sleeve: #f8f4ea, the sleeve front, the sleeve back and panels
        paleVinyl: #e9e4d8, the record
        groove: #cfc7b7, grooves and dashed rules, never text
        ink: #1a1a1a, text, buttons and playheads
        brown: #594f44, notes and day letters
        tangerine: #e0662b, the sleeve stripe and record label, never small text
        tangerineInk: #a8420f, track numbers and overdue
        mustard: #e8b931, the sleeve stripe and the hype sticker
        teal: #1f6f73, the sleeve stripe, this week wedges and focus
        dust: #857b6c, last week wedges
        green: #24663a, On track
        amber: #8a5000, At risk
        red: #a3271c, Behind
    type:
        Three stacks. Display uses Arial Black, Helvetica Neue at 900,
        Avenir Next, Arial in lowercase tracked minus 0.04em for the 64px
        album title, 56px figures, 26px brand and 22px side headings. Text
        uses Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Noto Sans at 16px with 1.5
        line height, 19px bold track titles and 11px bold caps tracked
        0.16em for small labels. Track numbers and percentages use SF
        Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 700 and 13 to 18px.
    layout:
        A header with a small record mark and the lowercase brand, pill
        nav with the current item filled black, a pill search, a black
        pill New project button, a round bell and a teal avatar with the
        user. The stage puts a square sleeve on the left and the record on
        the right, the record tucked a little behind the sleeve edge. The
        sleeve front has Brightwork records and a catalogue number, the
        lowercase album title good morning, mara, Released Saturday 31
        October 2026, three skewed stripes of tangerine, mustard and teal
        across the bottom and a mustard starburst sticker saying 4 tasks
        are overdue. The record is a pale disc with grooves and an orange
        label, holding fourteen wedges played clockwise from the top,
        last week in dust on the right half and this week in teal on the
        left, with counts at the tips and day letters around the label.
        The sleeve back lists the four numbers in a row over a heavy rule,
        then side A with tracks A1 to A3 and side B with B1 to B3. Each
        track has its number, title, percentage, team, tasks, due date, a
        playhead line with a ring at the percentage and the status. Liner
        notes list activity in two columns. Below 960px the record sits
        under the sleeve and the sides stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 40px sleeve padding, 14px per track and 40px between sides.
    density: Medium. One huge cover, then a compact back with six tracks.
    corners: Square sleeves. Everything you press is a full pill, and the record, label, swatches and avatar are circles.
    borders: 2px ink on controls, 3px ink rules on the sleeve back and dashed groove lines between tracks.
    shadows: The sleeve lifts with a long soft 40px shadow. No other shadows.
    icons:
        Solid simple shapes. On track is a disc, At risk a triangle,
        Behind a square and overdue a starburst like a hype sticker, each
        with its word.
    focus: A 3px teal outline offset 3px that follows the pill shape.
    tone: Record shop chatter with lowercase headings, such as side a, liner notes, Released Saturday and tracks A1 to B3.
